# AGENTS.md

An openElement application. This file is the entry pointer for AI coding agents
working in this project.

## Start here

- Agent and consumer index: <https://openelement.org/llms.txt>
- Getting started: <https://openelement.org/guide/getting-started>
- API reference (packages, exports, custom elements, config): <https://openelement.org/reference>
- Diagnostics (the `OEC` codes the compiler and runtime emit): <https://openelement.org/errors>

## Commands

```sh
npm run dev        # dev server with HMR
npm run build      # production build into dist/
npm run start      # serve the built output (and request-time routes)
npm run typecheck  # tsc --noEmit
npm run lint       # oxlint
npm run test       # node --test
npm run fmt        # oxfmt
```

## Project layout

- `app/routes/` — pages (default export) and form actions.
- `app/islands/` — interactive islands; each one hydrates with its declared strategy.
- `app/components/` — presentational components and their root CSS.
- `app/layout.tsx` — the shared document chrome every page renders inside.
- `app/head.tsx` — document head entries a config URL list cannot express.
- `openelement.config.ts` — framework options (head, i18n, middleware, ...).
- `public/` — copied verbatim into `dist/`.

## Rules

- Never edit `dist/` by hand: it is build output.
- Islands run in the browser. Importing `node:*` from an island fails the build
  by design — server-only code belongs in route loaders and actions.
- A page that mounts no island ships no island JavaScript; keep static surfaces
  static instead of widening the island graph.
- `dist/server/` is private server code; never publish it as a static asset.
- Keep `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm run test` and `npm run build`
  green after a change; `npm run check` is not a script in this scaffold.
